PKGSTATE_APPLY_ADAPTER(3)

# NAME

pkgstate_apply_adapter - admit completed application as native installed state

# SYNOPSIS

*#include <libpkgstate-apply/adapter.h>*

# DESCRIPTION

*project_completed_application()* validates a completed libpkgapply operation
against the accepted request, plan, target context, lease-bound state projection,
expected native snapshot, ownership universe, and completed path consequences.
It returns an immutable *state_publication_request* and performs no store I/O.

Install and upgrade additionally require *incoming_installation_authority*.
That value supplies an immutable *build_authority* admitted by
*libpkgstate-build* and, for initial installation, one installation reason.
The adapter verifies that the accepted planner operation names the exact admitted
artifact-content identity. Upgrade preserves the prior installed reason. Removal
rejects incoming authority.

Application admission never reconstructs build provenance from planner facts.

# OWNERSHIP

Complete object metadata comes from completed application evidence. Active origin
comes from the accepted active outcome. Rejected-object identity and side come
from durable completed rejected-object evidence. Publication fails when an owned
path lacks complete publication-eligible object truth or when application evidence
grants unplanned ownership.

# IDENTITY

Planner and application identities are translated into typed state references.
Source and build authority arrive through the already admitted build authority. State-owned installed control, receipt, package, snapshot, request,
and receipt identities are computed by libpkgstate.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgapply*(3), *pkgstate_build_adapter*(3),
*pkgstate_installation_receipt*(3),
*pkgstate_publication*(3)
